QNAP TS-328 voice prompts
=========================

What plays when:

- "Boot complete": once multi-user.target is reached (qnap-voice.service ExecStart).
- "Shutting down": at the start of every shutdown, reboot or poweroff
  (qnap-voice.service ExecStop). The unit is ordered after multi-user, sound,
  local-fs and alsa-restore, so it is stopped before all of them.
- "Powering down": on poweroff only. It plays from the systemd-shutdown hook
  qnap-voice-poweroff, the last userspace step before reboot(2). The kernel shuts
  the sound card down only after that.
- "RAID sync complete" and the RAID warning: from /usr/local/sbin/md-event,
  when mdadm runs it as its PROGRAM (see docs/INSTALL.md).

If there is no "RTD1295" ALSA card, the MCU buzzer is used instead:

1. the qnap-mcu input device (EV_SND)
2. otherwise /usr/local/sbin/qnap-mcu

Install on the NAS: `sh install.sh` (needs alsa-utils).
Settings: /etc/default/qnap-voice.

The prompts were rendered with Piper using the en_US-joe-medium voice and sox
(see render-prompts-piper.sh for the text and the exact settings):

    TTS_DIR=<dir with venv/bin/piper and voices/en_US-joe-medium.onnx> ./render-prompts-piper.sh [outdir]

Output: WAV, S16_LE, stereo, 48 kHz, with 0.2 s of silence in front and 0.6 s
behind. Piper's output varies slightly from run to run, so a new render is not
byte-identical to the shipped files.

Credits: Piper (https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl, GPL-3.0-or-later),
voice en_US-joe-medium, trained on the CC0 "joe" dataset and fine-tuned from
the CC0 "rdh" base model. The generated audio is distributed under the
project license.

Manual test:

    qnap-voice test
    aplay -D plughw:CARD=RTD1295 /usr/local/share/qnap-voice/test-tone-1k.wav
